id: pm-github-hptv
title: Bound native Bun CLI repeats of a completed public atomic import
description: "The intermittent historical installed-Bun repeat has not reproduced in three fresh packed repeats and three live-public-snapshot repeats. A real dangling comment-lock symlink independently reproduced an unbounded busy loop, fixed by honoring the existing wait budget. Installed acceptance retains its 45-second execution deadline and now force-kills the process group after a separate five-second cleanup window; timeout always fails even on a later zero exit. Recent repeats preserve durable bytes and strict health. The historical root cause remains unestablished."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T08:28:54.625Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T08:33:52.212Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[53]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T09:07:19.298Z",codex-sol,"A fresh bounded native Bun CLI repeat of the latest packed candidate passed in 4.22 seconds with exit zero and byte-identical tracker contents. This contrasts with the earlier long-running repeat, so retain the issue as an intermittent installed-host investigation rather than claiming a consistent Bun failure. All 375 native Bun library and operational tests also pass."
  "2026-10-05T09:55:33.050Z",codex-sol,"The final packed candidate matched all three authored runtime modules byte-for-byte. Its fresh Node public import passed with three issues, a byte-identical second run, zero gate findings, and strict health in 24.94 seconds. A bounded direct native Bun CLI repeat, using the same pinned host and startup executable path, timed out at 45.06 seconds and was terminated with SIGTERM; durable tracker bytes stayed unchanged. This reproduces the intermittent installed-host boundary alongside all 420 passing native Bun library and operational tests. No scratch remote was configured and no public-data push occurred."
  "2026-10-06T11:17:41.296Z",codex-sol,"Packed installed-CLI reproduction with the pinned host passes three consecutive native Bun repeats under the unchanged 45-second watchdog. The complete fixture test took 26.63 seconds, including packing, installation, Node import, and all three repeats; each retained item bytes and unchanged bare-remote refs. Separately reproduced a real dangling comment-lock symlink: open with exclusive creation returns EEXIST while stat returns ENOENT, causing the old immediate-continue path to busy-spin forever. The preserved fix adds sleep and checks the existing wait budget. This is a proven local lock defect, not yet proof of the historical installed-host timeout cause. Further public-data and diagnostic acceptance follows."
  "2026-10-06T11:33:55.510Z",codex-sol,"Fresh live public snapshot acceptance passed: one non-PR pm-todos issue updated since 2026-10-01, fetched with paginated gh reads, replayed unchanged through the packed candidate HTTP client and pinned host. Node import 2.49 seconds; byte-identical Node repeat 2.36 seconds; three byte-identical native Bun repeats 2.28, 2.03, and 2.33 seconds. Privacy PASS, strict health PASS, no remote configured. The complete all-state live import separately refused two email findings in older issue content before mutation, as required; no allowlist was added. Direct external HTTPS probes were intermittent, so the public snapshot receipt separates live retrieval from local installed-host execution. No deterministic SDK comment-add flakiness has reproduced; real create/comment/deduplication and permission-failure tests pass."
  "2026-10-06T11:37:10.437Z",codex-sol,"Acceptance now uses a shared process-group watchdog: the original 45-second deadline sends SIGTERM, then a separate five-second cleanup window sends SIGKILL. A timed-out command is always rejected, even if it exits zero afterward, and no writer step follows. The deterministic negative control uses a real CPU-spinning child that ignores SIGTERM; the watchdog force-kills it with unchanged durable fixture bytes. This bounds the historical installed-host timeout without claiming the dangling-lock defect was its original cause or increasing the execution deadline. The CLI lock defect itself now honors its existing wait budget."
  "2026-10-06T11:44:34.944Z",codex-sol,"Final frozen packed acceptance passes: one live public snapshot issue imported with gate PASS; Node import 4.02 seconds and byte-identical Node repeat 4.33 seconds; three native Bun repeats 3.36, 3.47 and 4.18 seconds with gate PASS and unchanged durable tracker bytes. Strict health passes in the disposable pinned-host project, with no remote configured. The spinning-child watchdog negative control also passes natively under Bun. Historical timeout cause remains unestablished; no deterministic SDK comment-add flakiness reproduced."
  "2026-10-06T11:52:11.132Z",codex-sol,"Native Bun full-suite negative control found a real HTTP boundary failure: a local server accepts the connection and never responds; requestOnce relies on ClientRequest.setTimeout(30000), but under installed Bun 1.3.5 no timeout rejection arrives before the existing 45-second test deadline. The identical full Node case passes. A fresh focused native reproduction is running. Stopped the superseded Bun release check so the transport fix can be verified on frozen source. This is an independently observed request-timeout defect, not proof of the historical public repeat cause."
  "2026-10-06T11:53:54.456Z",codex-sol,"Focused native Bun before-fix reproduction fails deterministically: one local silent-server test reaches 45.00 seconds without the 30-second socket-timeout rejection (38 unrelated tests filtered). Replacing reliance on ClientRequest.setTimeout with an explicit 30-second wall-clock timer, cleared on Promise settlement; the timer destroys the request and rejects directly. Regression now exercises two real responses concurrently: no headers, and headers plus a partial body that never completes. No execution deadline or test timeout was raised. Node and native Bun focused validation is underway."
  "2026-10-06T11:55:13.799Z",codex-sol,"The expanded native regression also caught a second concrete behavior: destroying a partial-response request before rejecting can synchronously emit response end under Bun, resolving the incomplete response instead of rejecting. The deadline callback now rejects first, then destroys. The real silent-server and never-ending partial-body cases test that ordering at the original 30-second limit. Node passes the expanded case; final native focused run and complete gates are being reverified. These are transport-boundary observations, not an assertion about the historical public-data repeat."
  "2026-10-06T11:55:38.455Z",codex-sol,"After-fix focused real-HTTP regression PASS under both runtimes: Node 30.02 seconds, native Bun 30.02 seconds; both silent headers and partial never-ending body reject with the expected 30-second timeout. The test keeps its 45-second harness deadline and asserts completion below 40 seconds. Build:test and ESLint pass. Explicit deadline rejection precedes destroy and its timer is cleared on every Promise settlement. Restarting full npm release checks and all native Bun files on this frozen fix."
  "2026-10-06T11:58:06.722Z",codex-sol,"Packed acceptance on transport-fix implementation 5ed8c47 PASS: one live public snapshot issue imported with gate PASS, Node import 6.17 seconds, byte-identical Node repeat 5.15 seconds, native Bun repeats 6.06/8.16/4.80 seconds with byte-identical durable data, strict health PASS and no remote. Timings include concurrent full validation load. The linked real timeout regression passes both isolated add verification and pm test --run --only-last --progress; it is recorded alongside the passing watchdog test. No SDK comment-add flakiness reproduced."
  "2026-10-06T12:42:46.684Z",codex-sol,"Final timeout assurance: full native suite passes 487/487 across 30 files with exit zero; both full release commands pass. The real silent and never-ending-body HTTP controls reject at the original 30-second deadline under Node and Bun; the dangling comment lock honors its existing wait budget. Packed public acceptance after the transport fix passes one nonempty import, unchanged Node and three Bun repeats, gate and strict health without a remote. Historical 45-second repeat cause remains unestablished, but acceptance keeps 45 seconds plus a separate forced-cleanup window and always rejects a timeout. No deterministic SDK comment-add flakiness reproduced."
  "2026-10-06T12:53:57.413Z",codex-sol,"Investigating PR #108 clone-only workflow setup failures. Plan: reproduce in a scratch clone, trace the npm lifecycle trigger and Git layout difference, isolate package preparation from the fixture tracker, then verify regression and full release gates in both layouts."
  "2026-10-06T12:56:15.328Z",codex-sol,"Reproduced the reported failure in a fresh clone with Node 22 and npm 10.9.8 after building. The failing command is npm pack --ignore-scripts in prepareWorkflowFixture, before pm package install. npm 10 pacote runs prepare despite ignore-scripts; npm 11 checks ignoreScripts and the same clone passes. The fixture passes its external PM_PATH into the package-root hook. Testing the worktree with npm 10 to verify whether Git layout is causal."
  "2026-10-06T12:57:10.585Z",codex-sol,"Confirmed npm 10 also fails in the package worktree with an external PM_PATH; Git layout and preinstalled merge drivers are not causal. The fix binds package packing to the package-local tracker and leaves caller import commands on their fixture tracker. Added a regression that forces the real prepare hook before packing in a fresh clone and a linked worktree, so npm 11 cannot mask the bug. The reusable caller workflow does not pack this source checkout and its npm ci/merge install run with its own repository tracker."
  "2026-10-06T12:58:11.661Z",codex-sol,"Regression verified red/green: removing only the package-local PM_PATH override fails with the reported outside-repository error; restoring it passes. pm test pm-github-hptv --run --match 'workflow packing isolates' --progress passed. ESLint and test TypeScript build passed. Running all three originally failing acceptance tests plus the layout regression under npm 10 in the worktree before pushing."
  "2026-10-06T12:59:01.408Z",codex-sol,"Both layout regressions fail on reverting the PM_PATH override, including the linked worktree with the pinned CLI. npm 10 exposed a second packing detail after fixing the root mismatch: successful prepare stdout contaminates npm pack --json by default. Packing now explicitly uses --foreground-scripts=false to preserve the JSON receipt; the regression also supplies a conflicting inherited foreground-scripts setting."
  "2026-10-06T13:04:14.167Z",codex-sol,"Worktree acceptance under Node 22.23.1/npm 10.9.8 passed all four selected tests: clone/worktree prepare isolation, all adversarial workflow cases, clean create/update review workflow, and the packed native Bun repeat with all three repeats inside 45 seconds. The complete selected run finished in 248.81 seconds under concurrent validation load. Implementation fd0834a is pushed; fresh-clone release gates are in progress."
  "2026-10-06T13:08:15.645Z",codex-sol,"Pushed CI run for fd0834a passes all 488 tests on Node 22 and Node 26, including the three repaired workflow cases. Both jobs still fail the strict coverage gate at 99.86 percent branches: index.ts lines 274, 4092, and 4117 are the successful gh credential-helper paths. Existing coverage depended on local gh authentication. Adding a deterministic synthetic gh auth success test with a mock server to cover these branches without host credentials."
  "2026-10-06T13:09:41.700Z",codex-sol,"Deterministic credential-helper regression passes directly and through pm test --run --only-last --progress. It removes both env tokens, shadows gh with a synthetic auth helper, checks trimmed-token Authorization at the mock API, and asserts token_source=gh plus credential redaction. ESLint and build:test pass. Obtained the exact CI Bun 1.3.14 runtime in disposable storage for final fresh-clone gates."
  "2026-10-06T13:18:34.181Z",codex-sol,"CI run 37468640976 at a849280 passes test (22) and test (26), including exact all-source coverage and the full native Bun 1.3.14 suite. CodeQL and the security scan also pass. Reviewer draft skips are not approvals. Fresh-clone npm and Bun release checks are still running locally with host GitHub credentials removed."
  "2026-10-06T13:28:14.761Z",codex-sol,"Final fresh-clone gates at pushed implementation a849280 PASS: npm run release:check under Node 22.23.1/npm 10.9.8, and bun run release:check under Bun 1.3.14 with Node 26.7.0 tooling. Both clones used an empty gh configuration and no environment GitHub tokens. Each passed 489 tests, exact all-source 100/100/100/100 across 12 modules, zero production audit vulnerabilities, package dry-run, changelog check, and publish attestation. Coverage receipts: 8398/8398 lines and statements in both; Node 22 has 209/209 functions and 2223/2223 branches, Node 26 has 208/208 functions and 2222/2222 branches. Packed native Bun repeats retained the original 45-second execution budget. CI test (22) and test (26) also pass. Only tracker receipts remain to commit; the historical intermittent Bun timeout cause remains outside this setup fix."
  "2026-10-06T13:52:24.540Z",codex-sol,"Review round 1: read all 16 inline findings and both review bodies. Verifying complete comment reads, diff hunk parsing, fatal Git decoding, canonical tracker paths, workflow credentials and pin grammar; adding revert-proven regressions before fresh-clone npm and Bun gates."
  "2026-10-06T13:58:29.574Z",codex-sol,"All 16 review findings verified valid and fixed. Every finding has a regression with a proven nonzero revert run and passing restored run; the two hunk findings share one proof. Real HTTP malformed and non-array second comment pages refuse both atomic and incremental gated imports with unchanged tracker state. Real tracked/staged invalid UTF-8 and symlinked-checkout cases pass. Credentials are step-scoped, install scripts disabled, checkout persistence disabled, and the branch lease uses checkout refs without a pre-push network read."
  "2026-10-06T14:06:25.566Z",codex-sol,"Full-suite validation caught a decoder correction: spawnSync can leave stderr undefined as well as null on ENOENT, so the Git reader now checks for an available buffer before fatal decoding and preserves the spawn diagnostic otherwise. The existing real missing-Git subprocess regression passes with the correction; tracked/staged invalid UTF-8 refusal remains passing. Superseded full runs were stopped and will be replaced by fresh-clone runs of the corrected pushed head."
  "2026-10-06T14:10:27.146Z",codex-sol,"Persistent revert receipts: 4196039888 workflow input shell; 4196039928 malformed second comment HTTP pages; 4196039937 and 4196078374 diff hunk content; 4196039948 tracked/staged invalid UTF-8; 4196078360 workflow credential isolation; 4196078420 symlinked checkout; 4196078439 pre-write command exit code. Each negative control exited 1 after reverting to the reviewed code, and restored code exited 0. The missing-Git follow-up also has an independent failing revert and passing restore. Selected native Bun 1.3.14 gate and workflow regressions pass."
  "2026-10-06T14:20:34.810Z",codex-sol,"Corrected implementation c8b9329 passes both fresh-clone release commands with 503/503 tests and no skips: npm under Node 22.23.1/npm 10.9.8, Bun 1.3.14 with Node 26.7.0 tooling. Both used empty gh configuration and no environment GitHub credentials. A new diagnostic assertion initially failed native Bun because empty PATH prevents the tracker read before generator startup; the fixture now separately injects generator startup and signal outcomes after restoring PATH. Node and native Bun pass this portable fixture, and reverting the diagnostic implementation still fails. Final pushed-head clones will reverify the bundled tracker receipts and test correction."
  "2026-10-06T14:33:50.266Z",codex-sol,"Final source/test head f572382 passes both fresh-clone release commands, 503 tests and exact all-source coverage. Strict clone health with merge drivers passes. Both CI Node jobs and native Bun pass. Local privacy separately audits 3581 objects, including unreachable objects, with approved identities and no secret/host-path findings. Separate upstream PM runner follow-up pm-github-2ao1 records a false empty_run on genuinely passing filtered Bun tests; the full 29-test native command is linked and passes. All 16 round-1 findings are fixed with verified failing revert controls. Items remain open and claims released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-06T15:17:49.785Z",codex-sol,"Review round 2 of PR #108: preserve published changelog binning through explicit item release metadata, add actionable diagnostics and real-shell rejection assertions for reusable workflow inputs, and strengthen the malicious-import tracker no-write assertion with a temporary injected-write negative control. Verify all release gates in fresh clones of the pushed branch; leave the item open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-06T15:19:21.145Z",codex-sol,"Findings 4197056035, 4197055992, and 4197056044 addressed. Set pm-github-7d1h release=2026.8.17 using the CLI and regenerated with npm run changelog:full. Compared every released section byte-for-byte with origin/main: identical; only the added Unreleased entry differs. Real workflow shell tests pass for numeric pins and every rejected repository/version/branch input with its expected ::error:: diagnostic. The adversarial tracker assertion now checks scoped porcelain stdout; temporarily appending a newline to fixture tracker settings made that test fail with M .agents/pm/settings.json and exit 1, then the injection was removed. Focused suite: 3/3 pass. Docstrings: 130 declarations in 11 files; lint, duplication (zero duplicates at the configured threshold), and typecheck pass. Fresh-clone npm and Bun release checks are next."
  "2026-10-06T15:36:25.199Z",codex-sol,"Review round 2 verified at pushed code commit 7a41660f190a108cca4bc10e270eff6b4864aa3e. Separate fresh remote branch clones installed dependencies with npm ci --ignore-scripts. Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check exited 0: 504/504 tests, zero skips/cancellations; complete coverage of all 12 authored modules with lines/statements 8406/8406, functions 208/208, branches 2225/2225 (exact 100/100/100/100). Typecheck, build, docstrings (130 declarations across 11 files), lint, configured duplication gate (zero duplicated lines), privacy (2829 objects), production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog check, and release-publish attestation all passed. Targeted review tests ran via pm test --run --progress and passed 3/3; changelog tests passed 3/3. Tracker write negative control failed as expected and was removed. All released changelog sections match origin/main byte-for-byte; no additional re-binned items. Full release receipts apply to the code commit; the follow-up commit contains only tracker evidence and claim release, with privacy/changelog verification to follow. No new blockers. Keep this item open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-06T18:23:39.081Z",pi-gh-cr3b,"Review round 3 (4 CodeRabbit findings from the 17:55Z full review) in progress on the package worktree. 4198811214: a fresh coverage run at the closing head re-measured 504/504 tests, exact 100/100/100/100, matching the close_reason receipt; the 503/503 in actual_result was the stale f572382 receipt. actual_result on pm-github-9cjx now cites 504/504 with the supersession note and the item stays closed. 4198811222: the degraded-mode lock test is split so its chmod 0o555 half and the stale-unlink permission-failure test skip visibly via node:test { skip } when process.getuid is 0, using the same non-root pattern the file already had. 4198811228: the source-slicing new Function test is replaced by a behavioral test of a new exported test/helpers read-only-directory helper that restores permissions in finally; coverage-remainder now uses the same helper. 4198811219 docs edit follows the remeasured counts."
  "2026-10-06T18:54:36.888Z",pi-gh-cr3b,"Review round 3 receipts, all four findings fixed at b446963 on feat/import-privacy-gate. 4198811214: fresh coverage at the closing head re-measured 504/504, matching close_reason; actual_result on pm-github-9cjx updated to 504/504 with a supersession note (503/503 was the stale f572382 receipt); item stays closed. 4198811219: docs/coverage-gap-inventory.md closing section marked historical (487-count receipts, pre-verification open note) with a current-status line citing the closed item, exact 100/100/100/100, and the closing 504/505 counts. 4198811222: import-lock permission fixtures now skip visibly via node:test { skip } when process.getuid is 0; the degraded-mode test was split so the file-parent half runs everywhere; nothing becomes uncovered because the fixtures still execute in non-root CI. 4198811228: the new Function source-slicing test is gone; the new exported test/helpers/read-only-directory.ts withReadOnlyDirectory helper restores the previous mode in a finally block, is used by coverage-remainder, and is behaviorally tested with a throwing callback plus mode-restored assertion. Focused receipts: node --test test/import-lock.test.ts 25/25; node --test test/review-round1.test.ts test/coverage-remainder.test.ts 21/21; both also pass under bun test. Worktree coverage at the final head: 505/505, zero failures/skips, exact 100/100/100/100. Fresh clones of the pushed branch: npm run release:check PASS and bun run release:check PASS, both 505/505 with the exact 100 gate, 130 documented declarations, zero duplication, privacy, audit, pack, changelog and attestation green; npm run changelog:check PASS. Follow-up pm-github-rap0 records the remaining root-sensitive helper-based fixture."
  "2026-10-06T19:48:30.209Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at 9a8620c (4 findings), handled by the orchestrator: (1) 9cjx description updated to the closing 505-test receipt (487 marked historical). (2) gate.ts git status/diff now run with --literal-pathspecs. Defence in depth: tracker paths always start with a directory, so leading pathspec magic was inert and git literal-matches existing glob-named files; the new guard test 'tracker file names that look like pathspec magic are still scanned' passed before and after. (3) README caller example no longer adds a caller-level concurrency block, matching docs/sync-workflow-caller.yml (the reusable workflow already serializes per repository). (4) Declined: restoring the old nested-directory fallback in resolvePmDataDir; the SDK resolvePmRoot is the canonical tracker resolution and a .agents/pm without settings.json is not a pm tracker."
  "2026-10-06T20:42:55.954Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at 7c425f2 (2 findings), fixed by the orchestrator: (1) absolute-host-path matched any slash-prefixed word, so GitHub slash commands (/assign), repo-relative links (/docs/setup.md) and API routes (GET /api/v1) failed --gate imports; the rule is now anchored to host-identifying roots (home, Users, root, tmp, var, etc, opt, srv, mnt, media, private, Volumes, usr, run, proc, data, nix, scratch, workspace, builds, Library, System) with a boundary after the root, matching the README's documented scope. Test 'host-path rule flags host-identifying roots, not slash commands, links or API routes' fails on revert; existing home/tmp/srv fixtures stay detected. (2) http-boundary timeout test now awaits server.close()."
  "2026-10-06T21:03:24.422Z",claude-orchestrator,"Follow-up to the host-path anchoring: the gate exempted 'structural' JSON-patch pointers (/metadata..., /body...) from host-path rules only because the old unanchored rule matched every pointer. With host-root anchoring no pointer can match (windows rule excludes a preceding '/', JSON pointers escape '~'), so the exemption was dead code. It is removed, and pointers are scanned like data (stricter: a secret in a field key is caught). Coverage back to exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-10-06T21:45:35.057Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at ed75fde (4 findings), fixed by the orchestrator: 9cjx description/actual_result/close_reason reconciled to 504/504 at 7a41660; canonical caller (docs + README) no longer hardcodes repository (the reusable workflow refuses foreign repositories and defaults to the caller); email-address rule exempts the git@ SSH service account (git@github.com:owner/repo.git) with positive control gitlover@; unicode-escape decoder uses a sticky regex instead of slicing the suffix per character (linear on large history lines)."
  "2026-10-06T22:03:02.088Z",claude-orchestrator,"Greptile 4200862803 on ae28d9e (valid, introduced by the orchestrator's git@ exemption): exempting every local part 'git' let 'Contact git@example.org' pass. The exemption moved from confirm() into the email pattern: only the SCP SSH URL shape git@host:<path> is skipped (negative lookahead requiring a path character right after the colon), with a lookbehind so matches cannot start inside a local part. Tests: git@ contact addresses (incl. 'git@example.org: thanks', 'agit@github.com:x') stay flagged; fails on revert."
  "2026-10-06T22:59:21.028Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at 194cf12, handled by the orchestrator: (1) parseUnifiedDiff skipped every line while no target file was set, so an operator --diff with a hunk after 'diff --git' without ---/+++ or after '+++ /dev/null' passed with an added credential. Hunks are now parsed even without a target, and added lines without one fail closed; genuine deletions still parse. Test cases in 'malformed, truncated, and binary diffs fail closed' fail on revert. (2) Two privacy-gate tests that write POSIX sh git wrappers skip visibly on win32 (CI is Linux). (3) PATH note on the no-git test: informational, no change. (4) hptv stays in_progress on purpose: it closes after PR 108 merges."
  "2026-10-07T00:23:51.656Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit 4201687009 (review at d7041ad), reproduced and fixed by the orchestrator: with a caller whose extensions.enabled list omits pm-github, the install edits settings.json and appends a workspace-history event; a no-change sync then failed with 'no item link could be generated' (and a real sync would have committed the setup change). The commit step now restores settings.json and history/_workspace.jsonl to HEAD (or removes them when HEAD lacks them) after the final gate. New workflow test 'an install-only settings change never reaches the sync commit' runs the real step shells from main with an explicit enabled list, asserts the precondition, expects exit 0 / no PR / no pushed branch, and fails on revert. Also added top-level permissions: {} (zizmor excessive-permissions); the job keeps its least-privilege block."
  "2026-10-07T01:12:40.286Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at 0f0c8c9 (2 findings), fixed by the orchestrator: README caller prerequisites now name the repository settings the review-PR step needs (read/write token permissions; 'Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull requests') and that GITHUB_TOKEN-opened PRs get no pull_request CI; test/helpers/bounded-cli.ts decodes child streams with setEncoding('utf8') so a multibyte character split across chunks is not corrupted. New test 'multibyte output split across stream chunks decodes intact' fails on revert."
  "2026-10-07T02:20:59.122Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit 4202386304 (review at d57335e): JSON object keys in history/planned records were never scanned (only values), so a token used as a key passed while the same text in .toon failed. Keys are now scanned as text. Test 'history object keys are scanned like values' fails on revert."
  "2026-10-07T03:21:18.330Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at 61b7ed6 (2 trivial test findings), fixed by the orchestrator: the githubHandler doc comment moved onto githubHandler (it sat above planEntry's), and the idempotency-refusal test now asserts the observable property (no 'plan verified' line before the refusal) instead of a regex that always matched 'Fetching issues'."
  "2026-10-07T04:27:56.381Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit Major 4203042480 (review at 08ca152), a real merge blocker: loadFixtureExemptions resolved provenance for every historical_test manifest entry via 'git ls-tree <commit>', and the pinned commit 434df42 is a branch commit that is NOT reachable from main after a squash merge, so the privacy gate would fail on main. Provenance is now resolved only for blobs in the audited object inventory (historical blobs vanish with the squash); present blobs with mismatched or unresolvable provenance still fail closed. The provenance test now covers both cases and fails on revert. Verified by simulating the squash merge in a scratch clone and running the privacy gate."
  "2026-10-07T05:27:52.940Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit Major 4203392922 (review at 66a3a43), reproduced and fixed by the orchestrator: in the gated non-atomic import, a failed update/close/reopen reconciliation only incremented 'skipped', and verifyImportedProvenance passed because the item kept its provenance tag, so the gated import (and the reusable workflow) reported success while the tracker differed from GitHub. The gated path now fails closed when the write count differs from the verified plan. Test 'a gated non-atomic import fails closed when a planned write fails' (one refused close plus one clean update) resolves successfully without the fix and rejects with it."
  "2026-10-07T06:31:48.660Z",pi-glm,"Review round follow-up (PR findings 4203767825 + 4203767821), pi-glm: (1) make syncGithubCommentsToAnnotations report a failed count (contended lock, unreadable existing comments, per-comment add failures) and fail gated imports closed when any planned native comment was not written or a created id was unparsable while annotations sync is on — both on the non-atomic and the atomic path; ungated behaviour stays warn-and-continue. (2) docs/coverage-gap-inventory.md: describe the 505/505 figure as a later-head measurement so it agrees with the authoritative 504/504 closing receipt. Regression tests go into test/coverage-remainder.test.ts with the existing helpers."
  "2026-10-07T07:11:31.984Z",pi-glm,"Disposition of both review findings (pi-glm): 4203767825 (index.ts) — VALID, fixed. syncGithubCommentsToAnnotations now returns a failed count (contended lock and unreadable existing comments count every planned comment; each refused add counts one). runImport accumulates the failures from every call site and an unparsable created id with annotations sync on counts the planned comments; both the non-atomic and the atomic path route the divergence through one shared failClosedOnPlanDivergence refusal with the existing \"planned write(s) failed\" wording, so a gated --comments-mode annotations|both import now rejects instead of exiting clean. Ungated behaviour is unchanged (warn and continue). 4203767821 (docs/coverage-gap-inventory.md) — VALID, fixed: 504/504 at the closing head 7a41660 is now described as the authoritative closing count and 505/505 explicitly as a later-head measurement. New regression tests in test/coverage-remainder.test.ts: \"a gated import fails closed when the comment-sync lock is contended\", \"a gated import fails closed when a per-comment add fails mid-sync\", \"a gated import fails closed when a created id cannot be parsed with annotations sync on\", \"a gated atomic import fails closed when committed items lack their planned comments\", and the ungated control \"the same comment-sync failures without --gate still import with a warning\". Two existing result-shape assertions (test/import-errors.test.ts, test/import-lock.test.ts) were extended with the new failed field. Each gated test was proven to fail on the reverted production code (4 rejected, control passed) before restoring the fix."
  "2026-10-07T07:11:36.590Z",codex,"Gate results (pi-glm): npm test 516/516 pass; npm run coverage exact 100/100/100/100 across the 12 authored modules; npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit zero (typecheck, build, docstring, lint, privacy, coverage, audit:prod, pack:dry-run, changelog:check, publish attestation all green). npm run changelog:check: Changelog is up to date. Open risk: none identified for this change; note the contended-lock regression tests each spend the ~30s import-lock wait budget by design (same as the existing contention test)."
  "2026-10-07T07:11:43.075Z",pi-glm,"Attribution note (pi-glm): the previous gate-results comment was recorded under a default author because the session author env was not exported in that shell; it is mine (pi-glm) and its contents stand as written."
  "2026-10-07T07:11:56.715Z",pi-glm,"Committed as 0ad387f (gate fix + regression tests), pi-glm. The doc-count fix follows in its own commit."
  "2026-10-07T07:12:00.358Z",pi-glm,"Both findings landed (pi-glm): 0ad387f fail-closed gated comment writes + regression tests; dc87f02 coverage-gap inventory now calls 504/504 at 7a41660 authoritative and 505/505 a later-head measurement. Pushing the branch now."
  "2026-10-07T07:31:19.560Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at 011f850 (2 findings), fixed by the orchestrator: review-PR bodies now add a 'proposed' link to each item on SYNC_BRANCH next to the permanent main link (main links don't resolve, or show the old version, until merge); the executed workflow test asserts it and fails on revert. docs/sync-workflow-caller.yml now states the 'Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull requests' + read/write workflow-permissions requirement."
  "2026-10-07T08:33:52.212Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit full review at 7e981cb (2 findings), fixed by the orchestrator: the three read-only-directory comment-failure tests skip visibly under root (closes pm-github-rap0), and executeWorkflow in test/import-gate.test.ts decodes child streams with setEncoding('utf8') like bounded-cli.ts."
